  "description": "PROPOSED PART SINGLE / PART TWO STOREY REAR EXTENSION, LOFT CONVERSION WITH REAR DORMER WINDOW, SIDE DORMER WINDOW AND FRONT VELUX WINDOW, FRONT PORCH EXTERNAL CHANGES, EXTERNAL CHIMNEY REMOVAL, WINDOWS REPLACEMENT AND TREES REMOVAL",
  "development_type": "Other house holder developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: [01, 02, 5, Design, Heritage and Access Statement, Fire safety statement, Flood Risk Assessment, Unnumbered Location Plan and Arboricultural Impact Assessment. Received 16/02/2026; 1 Rev A, 2 Rev A, 3 Rev A and 4 Rev A. Received 27/04/2026].\r\n\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building, unless otherwise shown on the approved plans.\r\nReason: In order to safeguard the appearance of the area.",
    "Condition : 4 - The windows formed in the west elevation roof extension shall be obscure-glazed and non-opening below 1.7 metres above internal floor level. The windows shall not be repaired or replaced otherwise than in accordance with the requirements of this condition. \r\n\r\nReason: In order to protect neighbours' privacy\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - The trees that are specified on the drawings hereby approved to be retained shall be protected before commencement of any works on site and throughout the course of the development by methods that conform to the best practice guidance contained in British Standard BS5837: 2012 or any guidance that shall have superseded it\r\n\r\nReason: In order to ensure a satisfactory appearance of the site and the area and to promote biodiversity.\r\n"
  ],
